   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let F be the antiderivative of \\( f(x) = x \\sin{\\left(x^{2} \\right)} \\) with \\( F(0) = 2 \\). Find the exact value of \\( F\\left(\\sqrt{\\pi}\\right) \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 3
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Let \\( u = x^{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Power",
            "x",
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Then \\( du = 2 x \\, dx \\), so \\( x \\, dx = \\frac{1}{2} \\, du \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Since \\( F(\\sqrt{\\pi}) = F(0) + \\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi}} x \\sin{\\left(x^{2} \\right)} \\, dx \\), convert the limits: \\( x = 0 \\) gives \\( u = 0 \\) and \\( x = \\sqrt{\\pi} \\) gives \\( u = \\pi \\), so the integral becomes \\( \\int_{0}^{\\pi} \\frac{\\sin{\\left(u \\right)}}{2} \\, du \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Sin",
               "u"
            ],
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "An antiderivative of \\( \\frac{\\sin{\\left(u \\right)}}{2} \\) is \\( - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Negate",
            [
               "Divide",
               [
                  "Cos",
                  "u"
               ],
               2
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 5,
         "text": "The integral is \\( \\frac{1}{2} - \\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right) = 1 \\), so \\( F(\\sqrt{\\pi}) = 2 + 1 = 3 \\).",
         "mathjson": 3
      }
   ],
